Usage:
  kumactl inspect [flags]
  kumactl inspect [command]

Available Commands:
  dataplane                 Inspect Dataplane
  dataplanes                Inspect Dataplanes
  meshaccesslog             Inspect MeshAccessLog
  meshcircuitbreaker        Inspect MeshCircuitBreaker
  meshes                    Inspect Meshes
  meshfaultinjection        Inspect MeshFaultInjection
  meshhealthcheck           Inspect MeshHealthCheck
  meshhttproute             Inspect MeshHTTPRoute
  meshloadbalancingstrategy Inspect MeshLoadBalancingStrategy
  meshmetric                Inspect MeshMetric
  meshpassthrough           Inspect MeshPassthrough
  meshproxypatch            Inspect MeshProxyPatch
  meshratelimit             Inspect MeshRateLimit
  meshretry                 Inspect MeshRetry
  meshtcproute              Inspect MeshTCPRoute
  meshtimeout               Inspect MeshTimeout
  meshtls                   Inspect MeshTLS
  meshtrace                 Inspect MeshTrace
  meshtrafficpermission     Inspect MeshTrafficPermission
  zones                     Inspect Zones

Flags:
  -h, --help            help for inspect
  -o, --output string   output format: one of table|yaml|json (default "table")

Global Flags:
      --api-timeout duration   the timeout for api calls. It includes connection time, any redirects, and reading the response body. A timeout of zero means no timeout (default 1m0s)
      --config-file string     path to the configuration file to use
      --context string         context to use
      --log-level string       log level: one of off|info|debug (default "off")
      --no-config              if set no config file and config directory will be created

Use "kumactl inspect [command] --help" for more information about a command.

